From 2893953809217dda39e1c0b0a41eabb54b8c856b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:55:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Choose among eight eggs when the partner dies: the four
 originals and the four hand-made Fresh babies

With NEW DIGIMON on, the egg panel shows two rows: the original four eggs (Botamon, Punimon, Poyomon, Yuramon)
above four new ones that hatch Pabumon, Pichimon, YukimiBotamon and Nyokimon (species 470-473). Left and right go
through all eight, up and down change rows; the panel is 96 pixels tall instead of 80. With NEW DIGIMON off the
panel, the cursor and the eggs are the original's. The death that picks an egg at random (no lives left) picks
among the eggs the panel would show.

The new icons and CLUT rows 497-500 are drawn into the disc's ETCDAT/TAMA.TIM at build time (tools/egg_art.py).
TAMA.TMD's buffer has 28 bytes to spare, so a new egg is drawn with the 3D model of an original group (Pabumon and
Pichimon group 2, YukimiBotamon group 1, Nyokimon group 0) and its row is copied over that group's CLUT row when
the hatch starts; the texture is loaded again at the next death.

REINCARNATION_STATS has rows for the four original babies only, so a new baby hatches with the row of the baby its
species file names as "vanilla_as", plus the inherited share as for any egg (the typedef moves to partner.h).

All of it is code in the DOO2 and DOOA overlays: no byte of the main executable.
